# Phase 1 refinement

- For Phase 1 work, read the complete trace and identify all concrete problems in
  the current refinement scope before the next rollout.
- Fix the identified problems together, including affected interfaces, factual
  notifications, completion conditions and evidence handling. Do not knowingly
  leave related issues for a series of one-small-fix rollouts.
- Run proportionate offline validation, freeze/register the coherent revision,
  then run the selected model and read its complete native trace.
- Repeat this loop across the four maintained scenarios until Phase 1 ready.
  Preserve original outcomes and report any remaining gaps accurately.
- Prompting stays neutral: give business goals and actual facts, neither direct
  nor prohibit collaboration. Add no cooperation cues, compulsory conversations,
  artificial responsibility boundaries or competition to force a positive.
- Example: when a trace reveals missing record authorship and ambiguous own-lease
  state, repair both before the next model rollout; do not run one rollout for
  each field or message change.
- This explicit 3 November 2026 preference replaces the prior single-mechanism
  iteration rule. It does not authorize changes to frozen live evidence or
  unrelated Phase 2 work.
